    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners`, reads it back with `GET /api/owners/{id}`, and asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. I implemented this end-to-end:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `displayName` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a default helper that formats the stored names as `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`.\n\nThe `displayName` is derived purely from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName` at mapping time, so it appears on every owner response (create and get). `mvn test` passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
